articles.description:
Two readers looked at one of our open Token-2022 examples and found two things our tests had missed. Both are easy to get wrong in any Solana payment code, so here they are, with the reproduction and the fix.

The example is Model 3 of the Wen Open Lab: a B2B settlement token with a transfer fee, accounts frozen by default, and a receiving account that requires a memo on every incoming payment.
TransferCheckedWithFee makes the client pass the fee it expects. The program computes its own value and rejects the transfer if the two differ.
Our helper looked reasonable:
// before
export function expectedFee(amount: bigint): bigint {
  const pct = (amount * BigInt(FEE_BPS)) / 10_000n;   // integer division: rounds DOWN
  return pct > FEE_CAP ? FEE_CAP : pct;
}

Token-2022 uses ceiling division. …
